  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Managing Recovery from Disasters in the Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Philippines is considered one of the most disaster-prone countries in the world. Due to its geographical location, both along the typhoon belt and the Pacific Ring of Fire, the country ranks among the top 10 countries most vulnerable to climate-induced geohazards. With the climate and disaster risks and vulnerabilities of the country, there is an urgent need for timely, well-planned, gender-sensitive inclusive intervention. The UNDP Philippines Country Office (CO) is implementing its Managin</narrative>
  </description>
